      "side": 1,
      "message": "This message is suppressed if you use the python-keystoneclient to update your password. For example, I did the following:\n\n- created a user with password\u003d\u0027password\u0027\n- used osc to update my password to \u0027password2\u0027\n- used osc to update my password to \u0027password\u0027\n\nThe error that I got back was \n\n Old password and new password must be different.\n\nBecause of:\n\nhttps://github.com/openstack/python-keystoneclient/blob/master/keystoneclient/v3/users.py#L220-L222\n\nIf I do the following:\n\n- created a user with password\u003d\u0027password\u0027\n- used osc to update my password to \u0027password2\u0027\n- used osc to update my password to \u0027password3\u0027\n- used osc to update my password to \u0027password\u0027\n\nI get:\n\n Invalid password: The new password cannot be identical to a previous password. Maximum number of uniqueprevious passwords required: 3 (HTTP 400) (Request-ID: req-e88d0239-72b0-4583-a795-9fb4c55ef7fc)\n\n\nWhich is definitely more informative. I wonder if we should patch the client to give this information in the first case, too?",
